{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":173136,"duration_api_ms":207115,"num_turns":5,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2f4bd907-1374-4d70-9a51-d995ce6cbf63","total_cost_usd":0.6084905000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25836,"cache_read_input_tokens":81227,"output_tokens":1646,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":148,"outputTokens":16363,"cacheReadInputTokens":1857915,"cacheCreationInputTokens":77982,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.365232,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":1646,"cacheReadInputTokens":81227,"cacheCreationInputTokens":25836,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24325850000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All three amendments are verified and well-founded. fr-2-7ec97029 confirms four dead `_volume_l` parameters in shrimp.rs helpers. fr-2-b9d261ac confirms the sole hardcoded Monod K constant in the nitrogen cycle. fr-2-7a74aad7 confirms a real zero-volume bug where rescale_totals_for_volume zeroes all dissolved chemistry when old_volume_l <= EPSILON after low fill_ratio geometry overrides.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7ec97029","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: all four private helpers (shrimp_feeding, update_condition, update_molt_stress, emit_molt_stress_warning) accept `_volume_l: f64` with underscore prefix and never reference it. Each uses TankState concentration helpers (tan_mg_n_per_l, nitrite_mg_n_per_l, do_mg_per_l, gh_d) or direct state field access instead. step_daily_shrimp passes volume_l to these functions but it serves no purpose — volume_l is only meaningful for the zero-check guard at line 66. Removing the dead parameter is safe, improves clarity, and prevents future confusion about whether volume_l should be used."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-b9d261ac","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: line 83 of nitrogen_cycle.rs has `do_total / (do_total + 2.0)` with a magic constant 2.0. ProcessParams has decomposer_k_doc_mg (default 5.0) but no decomposer_k_do_mg. All six other Monod K constants across AOB (aob_k_tan_mg, aob_k_do_mg), NOB (nob_k_nitrite_mg, nob_k_do_mg), and Comammox (comammox_k_tan_mg, comammox_k_do_mg) are fully parameterized in ProcessParams. This is the sole hardcoded K constant in the entire nitrogen cycle module, making it inconsistent and non-tunable. Extracting it to decomposer_k_do_mg restores the uniform parameterization pattern."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7a74aad7","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified as a real bug with a concrete repro path. In apply_startup_overrides, old_volume_l is captured at line 546 after geometry overrides (including fill_ratio) are applied but before substrate layers are replaced. With fill_ratio=0.1, fill_height can drop below the original substrate depth, making old_volume_l ≈ 0. When rescale_totals_for_volume sees old_volume_l <= f64::EPSILON, it sets scale = 0.0, zeroing all 17+ dissolved total fields (ammonia, nitrate, alkalinity, calcium, etc.). The result is a physically impossible state: positive water volume with zero chemistry. This silently corrupts the simulation. The fix should rebuild from the effective source-water profile for 0→positive volume transitions, and a regression test is essential."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"34ae78dd-e544-4f78-9a4a-213181da909e"}
